.TH SIEFS-DUMP 8
.SH NAME
siefs-dump \- show what is inside a SieFS image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B build/host/siefs-dump
.I image
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B siefs-dump
runs on the build machine (Linux). It prints both superblocks, then
every node of the trees with its items decoded (inodes, inline data,
extents, directory entries, attributes and their index, volumes), for
learning and debugging.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 1 if the image cannot be opened; 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR siefs (8),
.BR fsck.siefs (8),
.BR siefs (5)
